; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Kaleidoscope
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     symmetry, mirrors, random, polar coordinates, lists
; SUMMARY:  Draws random squiggles in one slice and mirrors them twelve times, like a kaleidoscope.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A kaleidoscope has mirrors that copy one small slice of colored
;   beads all the way around. This program invents a few random
;   squiggles and dots in a 30 degree slice, then draws each of them
;   twelve times: turned by 60 degrees six times, and each of those
;   flipped over as in a mirror.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Every run shows a new pattern.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * points stored as [radius angle] pairs
;   * rotation: add to the angle; reflection: make the angle negative
;   * drawing the same list of points many times with FOREACH
;   * building random lists with a loop
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 8 copies by turning 90 degrees instead of 60.
;   * Leave out the mirror copies. Does it still look like a
;     kaleidoscope?
;   * Make the squiggles longer by adding more points.
; ============================================================

make "beads [[255 80 80] [255 200 60] [80 210 120] [70 160 255]
             [200 100 255] [255 130 200] [250 250 250]]

; POLAR moves to radius :r and angle :a from the middle.
to polar :r :a
  setxy :r * sin :a :r * cos :a
end

; RANDOM.POINT makes a point somewhere inside the 30 degree slice.
to random.point
  output list (random 10 280) (random 0 30)
end

; SQUIGGLE makes a list of four random points.
to squiggle
  output (list random.point random.point random.point random.point)
end

; WALK.POINTS draws a list of points turned by :turn degrees. :flip is 1
; for the slice itself and -1 for its mirror image.
to walk.points :points :turn :flip
  penup
  foreach :points [
    polar first ? :turn + :flip * last ?
    pendown
  ]
end

; COPIES draws a squiggle in all twelve places.
to copies :points
  for [k 0 5] [
    walk.points :points :k * 60 1
    walk.points :points :k * 60 -1
  ]
end

; BEAD.COPIES places a round bead in all twelve places.
to bead.copies :point
  for [k 0 5] [
    foreach [1 -1] [
      penup polar first :point :k * 60 + ? * last :point
      dot pos
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [15 10 30]
repeat 10 [
  setpencolor pick :beads
  setpensize (random 2 6)
  copies squiggle
]
repeat 12 [
  setpencolor pick :beads
  setpensize (random 6 18)
  bead.copies random.point
]
